Considering I've also seen various monsters steal my cloak right off
my back, I'm not sure I can see the advantage in that regard. And I've
met many more clothes-stealing (or removing) monsters than ones
wielding bullwhips (although granted the ones wielding bullwhips are
usually rather nasty...).

The other dilemma with whether to wear the cloak of MR is of course
depending on what other equipment I have, I may prefer to wear a robe,
or displacement cloak or what have you.

The other option of course is GDSM instead of SDSM, but of course the
wizard's only other really usable option for reflection is the amulet,
and reflection, like magic resistance, is a highly desirable attribute
to have. And since the wiz's quest artifact is an amulet (can't
remember the name) you are at a further dillemma of which amulet to
wear (although I think the artifact can confer some benefits by simply
carrying it). (If I were playing another class it would be less of a
dilemma... wear GDSM and get reflection from shield or amulet, and
wear different useful cloak; this doesn't work for ALL classes but
most of the ones I've played).

I'm not exactly *arguing* with you here, I'm just pointing out in my
opinion it's not an easy decision to make, in the long run, of how to
equip yourself. And also very dependent on what other items you find
along the way in the dungeon.

I will absolutely agree--as I have done so already--I should not take
my wizard's cloak for granted, as I had apparently been doing.

I think somehow my erroneous disregard for the cloak was at times I
had gotten Magicbane very early in the game and at the time being
would have much preferred the added benefit of something like
displacement rather than having "redundant" magic resistance, not
thinking about its further use later on in the game. As it is, I shall
stand corrected.

